                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Third conditional and regrets",
                    "explanation": "El tercer condicional imagina un pasado diferente y su consecuencia, que tampoco pasó: If + past perfect, would have + participio. If we had checked the files, this wouldn't have happened.\n\nEn la consecuencia también podemos usar could have o might have: If you'd told me, I could have helped.\n\nPara lamentar algo del pasado: wish + past perfect: I wish I had stayed later. I wish I hadn't uploaded it in such a hurry.\n\nCuidado con la contracción 'd: en la parte del if es had (If we'd known) y en la consecuencia es would (we'd have stayed).",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Estructura",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "If + had + participio, would have + participio",
                          "If we had checked the files, this wouldn't have happened."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Negativa",
                          "If I hadn't been so tired, I would have noticed."
                        ],
                        [
                          "con could / might",
                          "If you'd told me, I could have helped."
                        ],
                        [
                          "wish + past perfect",
                          "I wish I had stayed later."
                        ],
                        [
                          "'d = had / would",
                          "If we'd known, we'd have stayed."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "If we had checked the files, this wouldn't have happened.",
                      "If I hadn't been so tired last night, I would have noticed.",
                      "I wish I had stayed later yesterday.",
                      "If you hadn't spotted it, we'd have been in real trouble."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Past perfect continuous: we had been working",
                    "explanation": "El past perfect continuous (had been + -ing) describe una actividad que duró hasta un momento del pasado, o justo antes. Sirve mucho para explicar causas: Daniel was exhausted because he had been working until midnight.\n\nCon for / since dice cuánto tiempo llevaba pasando: We had been testing the site for three weeks when we launched it.\n\nCompáralo con el past perfect simple, que mira el resultado o el número de veces: I had checked the files twice (resultado) / I had been checking the files all morning (actividad, duración).\n\nLos verbos de estado (know, be, have como posesión) van en past perfect simple: I had known Helen for years (no «had been knowing»).",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Causa de algo pasado",
                          "He was tired because he had been working all night."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Duración hasta un momento",
                          "We had been testing it for three weeks when it went live."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Resultado → past perfect",
                          "Daniel had uploaded the wrong version."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Verbo de estado",
                          "Helen had known Mark for years."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Daniel was exhausted because he had been working until midnight.",
                      "We had been preparing the launch for weeks when it happened.",
                      "Lucía's eyes were red. She had been looking at the screen all night.",
                      "Helen had seen the old version before anyone else noticed."
                    ]
                  }
                },
